"] " kept the US in the lead and " [:a {:href "/athletes/115618"} "Cullen Jones"] " extended that on the third leg. The anchor swimmers were France’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/125868"} "Yannick Agnel"] " and American " [:a {:href "/athletes/103585"} "Ryan Lochte"] ". They had swim earlier in the night in the 200 free with Agnel winning and Lochte placing fourth. Lochte was definitely stronger but not well-known as a sprinter and the question was if he could hold off Agnel."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The answer was no. Agnel closed quickly and won gold for France in 3:09.93, with Lochte coming home in 3:10.38 for the silver medal. Russia won a surprising bronze medal as they finished just ahead of Australia. For Phelps it was his 17th Olympic medal ever, and his first in London, but it was his first ever Olympic silver medal, after 14 golds, and two bronzes."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitors"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} "France"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/FRA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/FRA.png"}] "FRA"]] [:td {} "3:13.38 (1 h1)"] [:td {} "3:09.93 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {}] [:td {:colspan "10"} [:a {:href "/athletes/103437"} "Amaury Leveaux"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/103436"} "Fabien Gilot"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/115829"} "Clément Lefert"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/125868"} "Yannick Agnel"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/115781"} "Alain Bernard"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/125892"} "Jérémy Stravius"]]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} "United States"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.p